    "updated_at": "2026-11-14T09:37:12Z",
    "body": "Held work on issue/1605-import-guard-flake (commit pushed, no PR).\n\nWhat was done: the two pins bounded by an evaluation cap (lowered-cap refusal, and the may-jump refusal at cap 1 000) now use a 120 s hang barrier instead of 30 s. The cap stays the bound. The guard and the importer are unchanged.\n\nMeasured (debug, this machine): lowered-cap refusal 0.06 s; default-cap pin 52 s serial.\n\nWhy held: a full binary run in parallel threads with the new barrier passed once (50.53 s). A second run failed once, in 53.83 s, on a_finer_pass_that_runs_out_on_a_face_that_may_jump_is_refused. The failure was an assertion, not the barrier, and its panic text was not captured. The wait is not the cause. A 120 s barrier alone does not prove the flake is gone.\n\nNext step for the next worker: capture the panic text of that test under parallel load (run the binary several times, with output to a file), and check whether any shared state between parallel tests affects the may-jump refusal.\n\nLabel moved to effort:medium; claim released.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
