    "body": "Red occurrence, same 30 s cap family. Post-merge gate run 43584872633 on main 7c07e8683 (2026-11-14, 10:21-10:46 UTC) failed only `camcraft-app --test import_step_guard`. Two tests panicked at `crates/app/tests/import_step_guard.rs:36`: `a_lowered_cap_refuses_the_same_face_at_once` (the named flake) and `a_finer_pass_that_runs_out_on_a_face_that_may_jump_is_refused`. The message is the same: \"import did not finish within 30s - the hang is back\".\n\nReadings: the binary finished in 35.49 s; the two tests share the 30 s wait cap in parallel threads. The app-suites job took 963 s in a busy runner window (several pr-test reviews and the merge batch runs ran nearby). No other suite was red. This is the wall-clock cap under contention, not a new hang.\n\nPR #1652 (in review now) moves the heavy default-cap test out of this binary. If the same two failures recur on a quiet runner after #1652 merges, the second test's cap needs the same treatment.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
